  {
   "etapa": "explicar",
   "piezas": [
    {
     "tipo": "explicacion",
     "titulo": "Getting someone else to act",
     "texto": [
      "When you want **another person** to do something, you use **que + subjunctive** after advice, a request, a need or an order:\n\n- **Te aconsejo que** descanses.\n- **Te pido que** me ayudes.\n- **Necesito que** vengas.\n- **Es mejor que** lo hagas hoy.\n\nIf the person who needs and the one who acts are the **same**, use the infinitive: **necesito descansar**.\n\nWith **decir** there are two meanings: **dice que viene** is a fact; **dice que vengas** is an order passed to another person."
     ],
     "tutora": ""
    },
    {
     "tipo": "gramatica",
     "titulo": "Verbs of influence",
     "texto": [
      "These verbs want to **influence** another person and ask for **que + subjunctive**:\n\n- **aconsejar**, **recomendar**, **sugerir** → advice.\n- **pedir**, **necesitar** → a request or a need.\n- **ordenar**, **prohibir** → an order.\n- **permitir**, **dejar** → permission.\n\nThe pronoun says who it is aimed at: **te** aconsejo, **le** pido, **me** prohíbe.\n\nIf the one who asks and the one who acts are the same person, use the **infinitive**: necesito **descansar**. With advice and permission it is also possible: te aconsejo **descansar**.\n\nOther ways to advise: **lo mejor es que** + subjunctive, **¿por qué no…?** and **deberías** + infinitive."
     ],
     "ejemplos": [
      {
